{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Capability call sites are cast, not guarded — a non-capable transport fails silently\n\n## The gap\n\nTicket `cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8` annotated the core reconciler's `client`/`transport` parameters with\nthe `TicketTransport` port. Four call sites then reported `[attr-defined]` because they reach for\nOPT-IN capability members that the base port deliberately does not declare:\n\n| site (re-located 2026-08-11) | member |\n|---|---|\n| `dispatch_one.py:417` (`create_one`) | `add_comment` |\n| `dispatch_one.py:657` (`_update_one_scalar_update`) | `add_comment` |\n| `dispatch_one.py:742` (`_update_one_dispatch_links`) | `set_relationship` |\n| `dispatch_apply_phases.py:165` (`_update_one_dispatch_comments`) | `add_comment` |\n\nEach was correctly resolved with `cast(\"SupportsComments\", client)` / `cast(\"SupportsLinks\", client)`\n— correct, because widening to `Any` would have destroyed the enforcement cc77 exists to add.\n\n**But a `cast` is a static assertion with NO runtime effect.** None of the four sites checks that the\ntransport actually HAS the member. Compare `fetcher.py:597/647/688`, which gate the same class of\noptional capability on `hasattr` before calling. The reconciler is inconsistent with itself.\n\n## Why the failure would be silent\n\nAn `AttributeError` at any of these sites lands inside a broad `except Exception` on the dispatch\npath. A transport missing an opt-in capability would not crash the pass and would not surface a\nbridge alert — the mutation would simply never be applied, and the reconciler would report success.\nThat conflates \"capability absent (designed, fine to skip)\" with \"capability present but threw\n(a real failure)\". Same silent-soft-failure shape as `d067-5d2f-bcee-46ae`.\n\n## OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-12, on record)\n\nImplement the runtime guards AND report skip-vs-failure **distinctly through the EXISTING bridge\naudit/log channel**. Do **not** invent a new alert mechanism.\n\n- Guard shape: `isinstance(client, SupportsComments)` / `isinstance(client, SupportsLinks)` —\n  ADR-0083:193-198 prescribes `isinstance`-guarded capability detection against the\n  `@runtime_checkable` capability Protocols in `_backend.py`, and both are already\n  `@runtime_checkable`. This is a deliberate, documented divergence from `fetcher.py`'s `hasattr`\n  (which predates the Protocols and probes single members, not the capability); the divergence is\n  justified in an in-code comment per AC3.\n- Capability **absent** → explicit designed skip: an INFO log naming the missing capability and the\n  site, the sub-op still **counted** as computed (so it is queryable, never a silent zero), and a\n  durable record on the EXISTING `bridge_alerts` channel (`pass_io._load_alert_store()`, the same\n  store `record_parent_divergence` and `_record_reporter_alert` already write) under a **distinct**\n  kind: `outbound-comment-capability-absent` / `outbound-link-capability-absent`.\n- Capability **present but raised** → unchanged existing failure path: `logger.warning` /\n  stderr with the real exception surfaced, plus in-band `comment_errors` capture where that already\n  exists. Never swallowed silently as before.\n- `cast(...)` is NOT replaced by `Any` anywhere.\n\n### Module-size constraint (drives one structural move)\n\n`dispatch_one.py` is 796/800 LOC — 4 lines of headroom, and the CI module-size gate is absolute.\nThe guards do not fit. `_update_one_dispatch_links` (dispatch_one.py:702-796) is therefore moved to\n`dispatch_apply_phases.py`, which is an EXISTING call-graph seam, not a mechanical split: its two\nhelpers `_index_existing_links` and `_find_link_id` and its sibling phase\n`_update_one_dispatch_comments` already live there. Post-move: dispatch_one ≈ 700, apply_phases ≈ 320\n— both inside the 200-500 target band's cap.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — all four capability call sites are runtime-guarded with `isinstance` against the\n      relevant `@runtime_checkable` capability Protocol before the call:\n      `create_one` (add_comment), `_update_one_scalar_update` comment-fallback (add_comment),\n      `_update_one_dispatch_links` (set_relationship), `_update_one_dispatch_comments` (add_comment).\n- [ ] AC2 — capability ABSENT is a designed skip that is OBSERVABLE, asserted by a unit test: a\n      transport implementing neither `SupportsComments` nor `SupportsLinks`, driven through the\n      dispatch path, produces (a) an INFO log naming the missing capability, (b) a non-zero\n      `*_computed` count with zero applied, and (c) a `bridge_alerts` record whose `kind` is the\n      capability-absent kind. No `AttributeError` is raised and none is swallowed.\n- [ ] AC3 — capability PRESENT but raising is distinct, asserted by a unit test: a transport that\n      HAS `add_comment`/`set_relationship` but raises produces the pre-existing failure signal\n      (warning log with the real exception; `comment_errors` entry on the comment paths) and does\n      NOT produce a capability-absent alert kind. The two states are never conflated.\n- [ ] AC4 — the divergence from `fetcher.py`'s `hasattr` shape is justified in an in-code comment\n      citing ADR-0083.\n- [ ] AC5 — [operator-attested] mutation-checked: deleting the guard at a site turns the AC2 test\n      RED with a message naming the missing capability (the alert-kind assertion), not an incidental\n      `AttributeError`; verdict recorded as a comment here.\n- [ ] AC6 — `cast(...)` is NOT removed in favour of `Any` anywhere; `make typecheck` stays green.\n- [ ] AC7 — no `src/rebar` file exceeds the 800-LOC module-size cap after the change.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"dispatch or reconciler\"`\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q -k \"reconcile\"`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786505178345068001,"uuid":"7b5d65ef-6ffb-4eff-b2d8-d57ba424b4cb"}